url: "https://the-two-trials.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  A documentary apparatus for the two trials of Jeanne d'Arc, the trial of
  condemnation at Rouen (1431) and the trial of nullity (1456), with the
  years from Chinon (1429) between them, built from public-domain editions
  with the original (Latin, Middle French, German) beside a working English
  translation, every excerpt read against the page images: the
  interrogations, the Twelve Articles and the verdicts of the University of
  Paris, the abjuration, relapse and sentence (Quicherat I, 1841); Jeanne's
  letters and Christine de Pizan's Ditie (Quicherat V, 1849); the Journal
  of the siege of Orleans and Monstrelet's Burgundian chronicle (Quicherat
  IV, 1847); the friars Isambart de la Pierre and Martin Ladvenu before the
  inquiry of 1450, six witnesses of 1456, and the sentence of nullity
  (Quicherat II-III, 1844-1845). With a timeline, a Compare page, twelve
  plates, and an explicit list of what is not carried and why. The burning
  itself is not described. Companion game: En nom Dieu.
